-- Code of Practice for General-Purpose AI Models, Safety and Security Chapter.
-- Commitment 9 (serious incident reporting): the NOUNS, and nothing else.
--
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. No domain expert and no lawyer qualified in EU law
-- has read this against the source.
--
-- Seat: the provider of a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk, deciding
-- whether and how the Code binds it. Every fact here is one that provider could state.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/cop-safety-security-2025.txt
-- (pdftotext -layout of the PDF; src:N below is line N of that file).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `Nouns for Commitment 9`

-- Who I am, as the Code sees me.
-- "Signatory" is not defined anywhere in the Chapter, and the Chapter does not say
-- how a provider becomes one; it is asked as a fact.
-- "general-purpose AI model with systemic risk" is the Chapter's 'model' (Glossary,
-- p. 30) and a term of the AI Act; it is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `the provider's standing` HAS
    `I am a Signatory of the Chapter`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the model involved is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN

-- How my model stands to one kind of harm named in Measure 9.3, points (1) to (4).
-- Each point names two routes: "the involvement of their model (directly or
-- indirectly) led to" the harm, or the Signatory "establish[es] or suspect[s] with
-- reasonable likelihood such a causal relationship".
DECLARE `my model's link to a harm` IS ONE OF
    `no such harm, or no link to my model`
    `my model's involvement led to it, directly or indirectly`
    `I establish or suspect with reasonable likelihood that my model caused it`

-- One incident, as the provider can describe it for Measure 9.3's initial-report clocks.
-- The seven harms are the ones the four points name, kept apart because point (4)
-- names four.
DECLARE `the incident as I know it` HAS
    `link to a serious and irreversible disruption of the management or operation of critical infrastructure` IS A `my model's link to a harm`
    `link to a serious cybersecurity breach`                            IS A `my model's link to a harm`
    `link to the death of a person`                                     IS A `my model's link to a harm`
    `link to serious harm to a person's health`                         IS A `my model's link to a harm`
    `link to an infringement of Union-law obligations that protect fundamental rights` IS A `my model's link to a harm`
    `link to serious harm to property`                                  IS A `my model's link to a harm`
    `link to serious harm to the environment`                           IS A `my model's link to a harm`
    `the date I became aware of my model's involvement in the incident` IS A DATE
    `exceptional circumstances apply`                                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- The four points of Measure 9.3, first paragraph.
DECLARE `a point of Measure 9.3` IS ONE OF
    `point 1, critical infrastructure`
    `point 2, cybersecurity breach`
    `point 3, death`
    `point 4, health, fundamental rights, property or environment`

-- What I did about the incident, from which 'resolved' (Glossary, p. 32) is worked out.
-- NOTHING for a date means I have not (yet) adopted such measures.
DECLARE `my corrective measures` HAS
    `rectifying the harm is possible`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date I adopted corrective measures to rectify the harm`        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date I adopted corrective measures to assess and mitigate the related systemic risks` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- The nine items of information in Measure 9.2, in the source's order.
DECLARE `an item of Measure 9.2` IS ONE OF
    `item 1, start and end dates`
    `item 2, resulting harm and victims`
    `item 3, chain of events`
    `item 4, model involved`
    `item 5, material on the model's involvement`
    `item 6, what I intend to do or have done`
    `item 7, what I recommend the authorities do`
    `item 8, root cause analysis`
    `item 9, patterns from post-market monitoring`

-- The two reports whose content Measure 9.3 fixes. The intermediate report is left
-- out on purpose: it carries further information "as available", which is no list.
DECLARE `a report with fixed content` IS ONE OF
    `an initial report`
    `a final report`

-- What I do to find serious incidents (Measure 9.1).
DECLARE `my incident identification` HAS
    `I consider the exemplary methods in Measure 3.5`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I review other sources such as police and media reports, social media, research papers and incident databases` IS A BOOLEAN
    `direct reporting channels are available`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I inform third parties of the direct reporting channels`           IS A BOOLEAN
